rm="translate(10.5 12.75)"></path></svg><p class="xnocm68">Founded in 1998: a supplier that also runs networks.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq xqkpoqq"><h2 class="x2aydey">FTTH drop cable FAQ</h2><div class="faq-grid xeygohs"><div class="fibre-counts-faq xo4iwue fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">G.657.A1 or A2, which do we need?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">A2 holds the tighter bend spec and is what most indoor and in-home work actually needs. A1 has fewer requirements and is fine on a straighter run. If the cable is going round door frames and into a room, specify A2.</p></div><div class="all-dielectric-faq xo4iwue fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">Do you supply pre-connectorized drops?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">Yes, with OptiTap compatible connectors to IP68 and GR-3120. Whether that beats field termination depends on your crew rate and your volume, and we are happy to work the numbers with you rather than push one.</p></div><div class="lead-times-faq xo4iwue fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">What protects against rodent damage?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">The armored drop series, NSS and SS, uses spiral armor for mechanical and rodent protection. It costs more per foot and saves more per callout.</p></div><div class="north-america-faq xo4iwue fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">Can we reorder the same spec?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">Yes. Specs are held against your account, so a repeat order is a quantity and a date rather than a fresh conversation.</p></div><div class="x28dwco fb"><h3 class="xpwrat5">What is an OptiTap compatible connector?</h3><p class="x0y7wlf">OptiTap is the common name for a hardened, sealed fiber drop connector format, first designed by one manufacturer and now available as compatible connectors from several sources. It lets a pre-connectorized drop be plugged into a terminal outdoors, in minutes and without splicing. Vocom supplies OptiTap compatible connectors rated IP68 and built to GR-326 and GR-3120, alongside flat drop cable.</p></div></div><div class="custom-fiber-cta xjri1g2 fb"><p class="xdrf2xf">Need a Fiber Built to Your Exact Specification?</p><p class="x7efv2t">Fiber count, jacket, rating and connector, we can source and build any fiber optic cable to match your spec.</p><a class="talk-to-a-specifier-button x2urddb" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="xvkflym">Talk to a Specifier</p><svg class="xquoydi icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 9.75 0" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(3.75 12)"></path><path d="M 0 0 L 6.75 6.75 L 0 13.5 Z" fill="transparent" stroke-dasharray="" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="var(--icon-stroke, 1.5)" stroke="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 5.25)"></path></svg></a></div></section><div class="simple-footer-2 xzxrxrs footer-slot" data-pagefind-ignore><Footer footerTagline="Your partner for telecommunications and fiber optic supply." title="Quick Links" menu1="VOCOM AI" menu2="Services" menu3="RenOS AI Agents" link2="/vocom-services" link3="/vocom-ai-agents" /></div></div>
